From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:55:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: skip the register snapshot while the core or PHY
 is off

After a cable unplug power_on can still be set while the DP core and PHY are already off; dumping the registers
then reads an unclocked block and hangs the SoC. Check core_initialized and phy_initialized too.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 7f97a129c..9deb900d5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1028,7 +1028,8 @@ void msm_dp_snapshot(struct msm_disp_state *disp_state, struct msm_dp *dp)
 	 */
 	mutex_lock(&msm_dp_display->event_mutex);
 
-	if (!dp->power_on) {
+	/* after an unplug power_on is still set while the core/PHY are off */
+	if (!dp->power_on || !msm_dp_display->core_initialized || !msm_dp_display->phy_initialized) {
 		mutex_unlock(&msm_dp_display->event_mutex);
 		return;
 	}
